dpu: count real DSC blocks in dpu_encoder_use_dsc_merge()

Backport of the first hunk of upstream b6090ffb30f3 ("drm/msm/dpu: Fall
back to a single DSC encoder (1:1:1) on small SoCs").

This next-20241220 snapshot caught the DSC topology rework mid-flight:
dpu_encoder_prep_dsc() is already the final num_dsc-aware version, but
dpu_encoder_use_dsc_merge() still hardcodes num_dsc = 1, so with one
interface (1 > 1) it always returns false and DSC_MODE_MULTIPLEX is
never set.

With our 2:2:1 topology patch that means both DSC encoders get
DSC_MODE_SPLIT_PANEL but no MULTIPLEX: dpu_hw_dsc_1_2 then programs
num_active_slice_per_enc = slice_count (2) into each encoder while each
is fed only one slice's worth of pixels (1400px), and the pingpongs are
never told to merge the two half-streams onto the single DSI. Observed
on the SM-X800's 2800x1752 2-slice panel as the console tiled into a
2x2 grid of squashed copies.

Count the DSC blocks actually assigned to the virtual encoder, exactly
as upstream does after the rework.

--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/disp/dpu1/dpu_encoder.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/disp/dpu1/dpu_encoder.c
@@ -622,8 +622,9 @@ bool dpu_encoder_use_dsc_merge(struct drm_encoder *drm_enc)
 		if (dpu_enc->phys_encs[i])
 			intf_count++;
 
-	if (dpu_enc->dsc)
-		num_dsc = 1;
+	for (i = 0; i < MAX_CHANNELS_PER_ENC; i++)
+		if (dpu_enc->hw_dsc[i])
+			num_dsc++;
 
 	return (num_dsc > 0) && (num_dsc > intf_count);
 }
 
